  "id": "COMPOUND:24022 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Miyabenol A is shown to have a target relationship with CX-1 through multiple pathways, with Ataxin-2 and 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 acting as intermediaries. These targets are all implicated in the regulation of protein degradation and are linked to CX-1 via molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Miyabenol A may modulate pathways involving protein degradation, potentially by targeting enzymes or substrates involved in the ubiquitin-proteasome system. The presence of multiple targets that ultimately connect to CX-1 indicates a possible mechanism of action involving the regulation of protein homeostasis. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Ataxin-2 and the proteasome in mediating the effects of Miyabenol A, suggesting a broader impact on cellular processes.",
